  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Improved food and livelihood security in Bangladesh (BUET additional funding)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">International Training Network - Bangladesh University of Engineering and Technology (ITN-BUET) has been a CAFOD partner for over two years, since the beginning of the IFLS programme (Ban-09-01) funded by EC and CAFOD.

Over the past two years, ITN-BUET has contributed technical advice and training on the following: development and testing of low cost solar panels, training on the assembly and function of solar panels, development and testing of solar-based water purification systems, secondary data collection of salinity level, provision of user specific information relating to the location of the mobile phone owner and the mapping of cyclone shelters in the coastal zones. 

With this grant, CAFOD is supporting costs of two full-time Research Associates, to further develop the pilot model low cost solar panels and rain water harvesters with solar-based water purification systems. ITN-BUET will collaborate with Caritas Bangladesh, ADD and DAM in working with grassroots community in selection of beneficiaries and training of beneficiaries and partner field staff, etc. ITN-BUET will link national level research with field level experimentation through its research and technology capacity. The manuals and published materials produced in the last 12 months will be provided to the beneficiaries.</narrative>
  </description>
